00:41:57.000 --> 00:42:30.000
sharing negative information with students, with listeners, with viewers. Do these warnings work? And how do you think they're connected with the conversation we're having about trauma and resilience? Trigger warnings were born out of the idea that everybody's, well, there's a wise but idea that people have hidden traumas lurking inside them or past traumas that were unresolved and they're kind of somehow raw inside people. That's a very common, became a very common assumption. And the trigger warning idea emerged from that as a kind of a way to say, you know, if anybody's

